  "_about": [
    "PHASE 6 - entity-resolution trap set.",

    "The system NEVER auto-merges identities: every result goes to a human. So the",
    "two numbers that matter are measured separately:",
    "  must_propose      same entity written differently  -> must reach at least",
    "                    MEDIUM (a reviewable candidate), otherwise a real link is",
    "                    never shown to the investigator (recall).",
    "  must_not_merge    different entities               -> must stay BELOW HIGH,",
    "                    because a HIGH proposal is the band an officer is most",
    "                    likely to accept. This is the protected number: 0.",

    "Trap pairs deliberately SHARE an attribute (same vehicle, same phone, same",
    "location) so the test is hard: a resolver that merges on one shared field",
    "instead of weighing the name would fail here.",

    "Identifier pairs are checked against graph_ops.match_key(), which is the",
    "mechanism the graph itself uses to decide two PHONE / VEHICLE / ACCOUNT values",
    "are the same object."
  ],

